  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 312 PM CDT Tue Jul 21 2026\n\nA northwest flow pattern remains in place through much of the\nperiod with a broad flat ridge building through the\nintermountain west through late week. The ridge begins to build\nslightly further east into the central US into the weekend. A\nweak shortwave will drop southeastward through the area late\nThursday and bring a chance for some showers and thunderstorms,\nwith mainly dry conditions otherwise across the area. \n\nMuch cooler air aloft will keep temperatures cooler and below \nthe seasonal averages through the end of the week. Thermal\nridging builds eastward into the area with H85 temperatures\nincreasing back into the mid to upper 20s Celsius by this\nweekend with the heat returning to the area. Southerly flow off\nthe Gulf returns by late Sunday into early next week should\nallow the humidity to return as well.",
